1
00:05:34,285 --> 00:05:40,285
A murder in the past. A mystery in the future.

2
00:11:08,571 --> 00:11:14,571
Last Night in Soho is a horror, mystery film directed by Edgar Wright.

3
00:16:42,857 --> 00:16:48,857
A young girl, passionate about fashion design, is mysteriously able to enter the
1960s where she encounters her idol, a dazzling wannabe singer.

4
00:22:17,142 --> 00:22:23,142
But 1960s London is not what it seems, and time seems to
be falling apart with shady consequences.

5
00:27:51,428 --> 00:27:57,428
Eloise Turner, played by Thomasin McKenzie.

6
00:33:25,714 --> 00:33:31,714
Sandie, played by Anya Taylor-Joy.

7
00:39:00,000 --> 00:39:06,000
Jack, played by Matt Smith.

8
00:44:34,285 --> 00:44:40,285
Peggy Turner, played by Rita Tushingham.

9
00:50:08,571 --> 00:50:14,571
John, played by Michael Ajao.

10
00:55:42,857 --> 00:55:48,857
Jocasta, played by Synnøve Karlsen.

11
01:01:17,142 --> 01:01:23,142
Last Night in Soho is a 2021 British psychological horror film directed and
co-produced by Edgar Wright, and co-written by Wright and Krysty Wilson-Cairns.

12
01:06:51,428 --> 01:06:57,428
It stars Thomasin McKenzie as a naive teenager who moves to London to study fashion design; there she is haunted by visions
of Sandie (played by Anya Taylor-Joy), a glamorous young woman who had lived during the Swinging Sixties.

13
01:12:25,714 --> 01:12:31,714
The cast also features Matt Smith, Terence Stamp, Rita Tushingham, and Michael
Ajao, with Diana Rigg and Margaret Nolan in their final film roles.

14
01:18:00,000 --> 01:18:06,000
Rigg and Nolan died in 2020, and the film is dedicated to their memories.

15
01:23:34,285 --> 01:23:40,285
Following its premiere at the 78th Venice International Film Festival on 4 September 2021, Last Night in Soho was released
theatrically in the UK and the US on 29 October 2021 by Universal Pictures and Focus Features, respectively.

16
01:29:08,571 --> 01:29:14,571
It received generally positive reviews from critics, who praised its technical aspects, direction
and performances, while its writing received some criticism (especially the ending).

17
01:34:42,857 --> 01:34:48,857
The film grossed $23 million worldwide on a budget of $43 million.

18
01:40:17,142 --> 01:40:23,142
The film was nominated for two BAFTA Film Awards, including
Outstanding British Film and Best Sound.

19
01:45:51,428 --> 01:45:57,428
The film explores themes of london, england, nightmare,
go-go dancer, time travel, nostalgia.

20
01:51:25,714 --> 01:51:31,714
The tone is mind_bending and dark and intense.
